{
 "method": "Prior shift applied to the published confusion matrices. Per-class recall is held fixed and the class prior is replaced; accuracy, precision and F1 are recomputed from the reweighted joint. Nothing is re-predicted. The assumption is that the distribution of text *within* a language does not change with the prior, which is the standard prior-shift assumption and is not tested here.",
 "why": "Every accuracy in the comparison is over a roughly balanced test set, and text does not arrive balanced. Precision on a rare class is the metric a balanced benchmark flatters most, because the false positives leaking in from a class a hundred times larger are not in the test set.",
